## Risks & traps (carried from the handoffs — read before each phase)

- `ok:true` is not "it ran" — always read `detail` on `/health` (`cache_sweep`, `synthesis` both report disabled-but-ok).
- The local clone is shallow and stale — `git fetch origin main` before trusting any ref.
- `deno test` rewrites `deno.lock` — check `git status` before staging.
- SQL three-valued logic drops NULL rows from breakdown queries — wrap in `coalesce(..., false)`.
- Write the negative control first (the 2-person/7-rows collapse-threshold trap).
- Edge changes deploy only via the Lovable mirror; the only proof of deploy is a moved `/health` SHA. `deployed_bytes_verified` is false — the marker proves provenance, not byte identity.
- A second agent writes to the mirror — sync only files that actually changed; never blanket-overwrite.

